From 76c2733074c58c71948be1cc4a4ee7665e5433b1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Michael Stufflebeam <cpuchip@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 17:19:43 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 5/5] 055 (5/5): the wasm gate, and 055's work file

games-wasm-gate.list lists BABAL, BABLW (Babal built as WebAssembly, stu32-arcade 3d522d5) and TRAP (stu32-arcade
12b36aa), for STU_WASM builds only; games.list lists no wasm game. device/standin/wasm.txt runs them through the
keys: BABAL and BABLW with keys held and FRAMEBENCH, then TRAP, whose key 0 recurses 100 deep and returns and whose
key 1 never stops and must trap; then C, and 2 ENTER 3 + still gives 5. The calc task's stack-free in each X line
is the figure soroban's calc-task ruling rests on (#5501), and TRAP stays in the gate so a later change to the
guard or the bridge shows. run.sh takes GAMES_LIST (default games.list):
STU_WASM=1 GAMES_LIST=games-wasm-gate.list device/standin/run.sh PORT device/standin/wasm.txt

work/055-wasm-apps.md: the decision 68 table (resources.py off and on, the per-game row, the board figures), the
gate, and what is open.

Written by arcade for soroban's gate.

Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
